I did not try your example, but I see a potential numerical issue here:

res(i) = 0;
for (int j = 0; j < means.size(); j++)
{
  res(i) += prop(j)*dnorm(lw(i), means(j), sigma(j), false);
}

You might consider doing the accumulation in log-space:

logres(i) = -INFINITY;

for (int j = 0; j < means.size(); j++) {

  Type log_increment = log(prop(j)) + dnorm(lw(i), means(j), sigma(j), true);
  logres(i) = logspace_add(logres(i), log_increment);

}

