Is it possible to estimate a model for a dependent variable that is k-truncated with k>0, in glmmTMB? I am working with a data set with a count variable for which the exact value is not known if it is 4 or below. The reason for this is protection of privacy, the data set is aggregated from data on individuals that are considered at risk of identification if there are few individuals within one specific institution one particular year. Apart from this the data set is suitable for analysis with glmmTMB, there are a number of institutions and observations for multiple years within each institution. Since this is a question of whether it is possible to estimate a specific type of model I do not included a data set here, but if preferable I may prepare an example where the problem is "solved" by a not particularly satisfactory ad hoc procedure by setting all such values equal to 2.

